WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.759
The promise of pretraining is that a model learns
general knowledge once from huge unlabeled data,

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.666
then transfers it to many tasks.

00:00:07.746 --> 00:00:11.003
The authors ask whether this recipe can work for tables.

00:00:11.083 --> 00:00:15.769
Three ingredients are needed: a way to represent
any table regardless of schema,

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:19.166
a training framework flexible enough for many objectives,

00:00:19.246 --> 00:00:22.264
and a data source large enough to pretrain at scale.

00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:26.316
Together, one tabular model could handle
classification, regression,

00:00:26.396 --> 00:00:31.142
missing-value imputation, zero-shot prediction, and
tables that grow new columns,

00:00:31.222 --> 00:00:32.870
without redesigning per task.
